one idea here: on Jenkins we can search a branch with corresponding Jira ticket number and check against it.
e.g.
If other queries from metadata.json define features with the same name – fail; 
If there are new features, but no server PR – fail;
If sth missing in server PR (feature definitions, encodings) – fail;

example:



{noformat}  dimension: is_latest_snapshot {
    type: string
    sql: CASE WHEN ${TABLE}.snapshot_date=(select DATE_ADD('MONTH', -1, max(snapshot_date)) from fpa_rides.rides_agg_snapshot) THEN 'True' ELSE 'False' END ;;
  }{noformat}



takes last max snapshot and subtracts 1 month because we are comparing snapshot to last actuals month.

